Text:
  A continuous image of a compact set is compact.
  Both topologies are explicit; no separation assumption is needed.

Result continuous image of a compact set:
  Attribution: mathlib; IsCompact.image; adapted
  Let X,Y: Type
  Let t: Topology(X)
  Let u: Topology(Y)
  Let f: Function(X,Y)
  Let S: Set(X)
  Assume continuous between(f,t,u), compact in(S,t)
  Conclude: compact in(image(f,S),u)

